From cb654e5623f0ea5b618a2b747d7c855111bc8fe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:56:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 40/42] power: supply: smb347: don't cache the command
 registers

The command registers (CMD_A, CMD_B, CMD_C) hold the charger's runtime
state: charge enable, the write enable for the configuration registers,
OTG, and the USB5/1/HC input mode. The charger resets them by itself, at
power-on reset and, as seen on the Samsung Galaxy Tab 2 10.1, when its
input power drops out: after a USB disconnect or a sag of the input,
CMD_B reads 0 (USB1 mode, 100 mA input) while the regmap cache still
holds the old value.

Since the switch to the generic regmap cache, these registers are
cached, so regmap_update_bits() compares against the stale value and
skips the write. On the tablet, writing input_current_limit then has no
effect: the chip stays in USB1 mode (STAT_E, and so the property, reports
100 mA), and with a system load of about 0.5 A the battery drains while
the charger is online. The same goes for charge enable (CMD_A) after
such a reset.

Mark the command registers volatile, so that updates read the hardware.

Fixes: 17e7bc532cd5 ("power: supply: smb347-charger: Utilize generic regmap caching")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c
index b3d47ec2ced8..435c9afdf32f 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c
@@ -1356,6 +1356,14 @@ static int smb347_property_is_writeable(struct power_supply *psy,
 static bool smb347_volatile_reg(struct device *dev, unsigned int reg)
 {
 	switch (reg) {
+	/*
+	 * The charger resets the command registers by itself: at power-on
+	 * reset, and on some boards when its input power goes away. A cached
+	 * copy would then make regmap skip writes that are still needed.
+	 */
+	case CMD_A:
+	case CMD_B:
+	case CMD_C:
 	case IRQSTAT_A:
 	case IRQSTAT_C:
 	case IRQSTAT_D:
-- 
2.55.0

